WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.568
-Our guest tonight
is an Emmy-nominated comedian

00:00:02.568 --> 00:00:03.970
for her work
on "Saturday Night Live."

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:07.073
She hosts and executive-produces
"Supermarket Sweep,"

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:08.707
which airs Sunday nights on ABC.

00:00:08.707 --> 00:00:09.842
Please welcome back to the show

00:00:09.842 --> 00:00:11.344
our very good friend
Leslie Jones!

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:12.778
How are you, Leslie?

00:00:12.778 --> 00:00:18.084
-What's up, Seth, baby?!
-Oh! I miss you, Leslie.

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:19.485
It's great to see you,
but I, of course,

00:00:19.485 --> 00:00:20.886
wish you were here in person.

00:00:20.886 --> 00:00:23.222
How are you feeling this
morning -- or this afternoon?

00:00:23.222 --> 00:00:25.825
-I'm great. I'm great.
It's nice and sunny out here.

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:28.428
See all that sun in the back?
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:30.062
-That's right --
you're an L.A. person now.

00:00:30.062 --> 00:00:32.699
Does that mean
you voted in California?

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:35.234
-Why you got to ask me
that on air? Why?

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:37.070
-[ Laughs ]
-Why?

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.371
Why you got to ask me that?

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.006
You ask the white people that,
Seth?

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:42.308
Oh, yeah.
I'm taking it there early.

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:44.010
-I -- We just have
a few questions

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:47.313
about some discrepancies
with your registration.

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:48.581
Ms. Jones...

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:49.949
[ Both laugh ]
-Were you --

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:52.152
-I think I did some mail-in
[bleep].

00:00:52.152 --> 00:00:55.388
-Did you -- Do you enjoy
watching results come in?

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:58.691
Do you like -- Do you like
looking at the maps on CNN?

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:01.260
-Well, I just was telling --
telling your people --

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:03.663
I was like, "It's like waiting
on a STD test."

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:06.232
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:10.136
-"Do I got it, man?
Do I got it?!"

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:12.772
-But you feel -- You're feeling
like you probably don't have it.

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:14.306
Is that where
we're at right now?

00:01:14.306 --> 00:01:16.242
-I'm feeling like the test
is going to come back my way.

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:17.443
-That's good.
-You know?

00:01:17.443 --> 00:01:20.747
-That's good.
Do you -- It is so much.

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:22.715
I feel like now it's like
a show for TV.

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:26.285
You know, John King at CNN,
he's turning the maps.

00:01:26.285 --> 00:01:27.987
Steve Kornacki over at MSNBC.
-I hate --

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:29.588
I hate them weathermen.
They are weathermen.

00:01:29.588 --> 00:01:30.690
-[ Laughs ]
-That's what they are.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.091
And you know what's so upsetting

00:01:32.091 --> 00:01:34.460
is watching them
trying to work the monitor,

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:35.995
and then they push
the wrong button.

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:38.864
You'd be like, "Yeah, 'cause
you're trying to be impressive,

00:01:38.864 --> 00:01:42.501
and you're not impressive,
okay?!"

00:01:42.501 --> 00:01:44.036
Stop with the weatherman stuff.

00:01:44.036 --> 00:01:45.271
And then they get
the marker stuff.

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:47.039
It's so annoying.
It's annoying.

00:01:47.039 --> 00:01:48.841
You know what I really hate,
Seth?

00:01:48.841 --> 00:01:50.142
Seth.
-Yep.

00:01:50.142 --> 00:01:51.210
-And I love the Cuomo.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:52.778
I love me some Cuomo.
-Yeah.

00:01:52.778 --> 00:01:55.481
-But when they walk
across that floor --

00:01:55.481 --> 00:01:57.984
when they walk across that floor
while they're giving the report

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:59.118
like they're doing something

00:01:59.118 --> 00:02:00.820
really, really, really
important,

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:03.756
like they're going to talk to
somebody else across the room --

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:05.625
Seth, I want to run up there.

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:06.859
I want to run up there, Seth.

00:02:06.859 --> 00:02:08.428
I hate that part.

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:10.162
-I know what you're talking
about, where they're like,

00:02:10.162 --> 00:02:11.731
"Let's go.
We're going to walk over

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:12.865
to John King at the map."
-Oh, it's....

00:02:12.865 --> 00:02:14.367
-You don't like
the walk and talk.

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:16.035
-And then the camera does that
swift thing behind their back

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:18.337
like they're --
it makes me want to --

00:02:18.337 --> 00:02:20.940
You're not important!
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.109
And you're telling me
the same thing you told me

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:24.877
five seconds ago.

00:02:24.877 --> 00:02:26.078
-Yeah.
-Okay, he got Michigan.

00:02:26.078 --> 00:02:30.183
Okay, he got Michigan.
Okay, he got Michigan!

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:34.220
-So [Chuckling] Leslie,
you -- did you --

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.022
-And, Seth, can we get
"American Idol"

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:37.823
to help them get
the results faster?

00:02:37.823 --> 00:02:39.392
How "American Idol"
can get their stuff

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:41.561
in one night and you can't?

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:43.329
-What about --
Did you watch --

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:44.864
There was a very strange thing
that happened last night

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:48.368
that, obviously, both candidates
gave speeches late in the night.

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:50.870
Did you watch those?
Were you up for that?

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:53.306
-Yes.
I had to watch the speeches.

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:57.109
Okay, first, Joe Biden comes out
with the speech that we need --

00:02:57.109 --> 00:02:58.477
like, be patient,

00:02:58.477 --> 00:03:01.014
which is very upsetting again,
America,

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:03.016
that we got to be told
to be patient

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:05.417
on some stuff
we've been doing for years.

00:03:05.417 --> 00:03:07.953
You let one person come up here,
an idiot,

00:03:07.953 --> 00:03:09.822
and tell us something
about the rules --

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:11.724
something we've been doing
for years --

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:13.626
and then, all of a sudden,
it's something different.

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:16.261
So we got to be tell people
to be patient,

00:03:16.261 --> 00:03:17.263
which is so annoying.

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:18.998
Grow up, America.
Grow up.

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:21.033
But even on the other side,
I am like,

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:23.002
"You know, how did
'American Idol' do that?"

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:27.440
Anyway, when Trump came up,
though, I was like --

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:30.342
have you ever just seen a kid
that is just mad

00:03:30.342 --> 00:03:32.277
because somebody
don't like them?

00:03:32.277 --> 00:03:34.513
Like, he had this little paper
and everything.

00:03:34.513 --> 00:03:35.948
He was like, "Yeah, we're gonna
take this to the court.

00:03:35.948 --> 00:03:37.182
We're gonna take..."

00:03:37.182 --> 00:03:40.519
And I'm just like,
"Oh, get out, please.

00:03:40.519 --> 00:03:43.155
Please, just get out."

00:03:43.155 --> 00:03:44.490
-He also sort of --

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.592
he basically announced
that he had won.

00:03:46.592 --> 00:03:48.628
-And he didn't.
-And what do you think

00:03:48.628 --> 00:03:52.398
about that play,
with so many states undecided?

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:54.000
-Well, it's just like --

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.901
this is what I've been saying
all along, Seth.

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:57.870
This is why I love you
and "Closer Look,"

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:00.306
because you nail it on the head
when --

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:03.409
He's just -- He's just doing
that celebrity thing

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:05.778
with the hands
and the cues and the --

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:07.379
and the repeating himself.

00:04:07.379 --> 00:04:09.015
And of course he comes out

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:11.450
and he puts these ideas
in your head.

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:13.352
And if you say it enough,
it's like --

00:04:13.352 --> 00:04:15.622
okay, it's like when they want
a hit on the radio,

00:04:15.622 --> 00:04:17.290
and they play the hit
like every --

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:18.757
like two times an hour.

00:04:18.757 --> 00:04:19.959
And you keep hearing it --

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:21.761
you know you don't
like that song.

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:23.362
You know you don't like
the "Shape of You."

00:04:23.362 --> 00:04:24.864
You know you don't
like that song.

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:27.032
Okay.
But it plays three times.

00:04:27.032 --> 00:04:28.901
So now I like the
"Shape of You" now.

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:30.236
Now I like the "Shape of You."

00:04:30.236 --> 00:04:32.104
Okay?
So that's what Trump does.

00:04:32.104 --> 00:04:34.340
Like, "Oh, yeah, it's a fraud.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.009
It's a fraud.
It's a fraud."

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:37.377
So you put that in your head

00:04:37.377 --> 00:04:41.013
of people who are not taking
time to think

00:04:41.013 --> 00:04:43.415
about the democracy
of this country.

00:04:43.415 --> 00:04:47.319
Yeah, he's doing --
he's doing entertainment 101.

00:04:47.319 --> 00:04:48.921
That's all Trump is doing.

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:50.322
-I want to ask you
this question.

00:04:50.322 --> 00:04:53.191
You and I are both --
we've both been very honored

00:04:53.191 --> 00:04:55.928
over the years to get
nominated for an Emmy or two.

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:58.664
-Yeah.
-We haven't won them.

00:04:58.664 --> 00:04:59.832
Have you ever thought that
you should have

00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:01.200
played it that way
on Emmy night,

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.702
and just shown up
at the red carpet

00:05:02.702 --> 00:05:05.271
and just started talking about
the fact that you'd won it?

00:05:05.271 --> 00:05:07.973
-Well, we already seen
Kanye kind of do it.

00:05:07.973 --> 00:05:09.875
You know what I'm saying?
You remember when Kanye

00:05:09.875 --> 00:05:11.110
ran up on the stage
and was like,

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:12.412
"no, we won."

00:05:12.412 --> 00:05:14.713
[ Laughter ]
Like...

00:05:14.713 --> 00:05:15.848
And, you know,

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:17.483
you could probably
get away with that, Seth.

00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:18.684
You could probably do that.

00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:20.486
But if I ran up onstage

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:23.155
and snatched a statue
from somebody white,

00:05:23.155 --> 00:05:26.925
they would beat me like
I had broke into Walmart

00:05:26.925 --> 00:05:29.228
and not tried to pay
at the regular register.

